  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 241 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe broad upper-level ridge will remain centered over the vicinity \nof the Carolinas and the Tennessee Valley Thursday and Friday. The \nridge axis will nose westward into the southern Plains through the \nend of the week, allowing for continued hot temperatures in the 90s \nto around 103 degrees Thursday and Friday. The ridge is forecast to \nbuild westward and become centered over the southern High Plains \nthis weekend into Monday of next week. Temperatures remain above \nnormal Saturday-Monday with highs still reaching into the mid 90s to \naround 100 degrees for most. Overnight lows will continue to range \nin the 70s for most places, except 60s in the higher terrain.\nIsolated afternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms will\nremain possible over the higher elevations of the western CWA each\nday.",
